[size=5][b]Every mod key and controller button, rebindable in the game's own Key Bindings menu.[/b][/size]

The game only lets you rebind its own keyboard keys, and many mods keep theirs in input files or [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/4885]Mod Settings[/url], or hardcode them. Unified Keybinds adds a section per installed mod to [b]Settings > Controls > Key Bindings[/b], built from your mods at every startup, so you rebind everything in one place, with a keyboard or a controller.

[i]Formerly Native Mod Keybinds. Files and folders keep their names, so updating works as before.[/i]

[size=4][b]Features[/b][/size]
Keyboard on the left, controller on the right in the images (stacked in the inventory hints).
[list]
[*]One section per mod, named from the mod's files, for example [i]"Mod: [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/5208]Let There Be Flight[/url]"[/i] with [i]"Vehicle Flight Linear Brake"[/i]. Add or remove a mod and the sections follow. Keys a mod never made rebindable are listed too, for example [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/11765]Enhanced Vehicle System[/url]'s F1 to F4.
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kaporli/unified-keybinds/main/screenshots/key-bindings-mod-sections.jpg[/img][/*]
[*]Entries for keys the game and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/4008]No More Hard-coded Keybinds[/url] fixed: Confirm, Cancel, Track Waypoint, Cycle Objective, Disassemble, Drop, Unequip, Enable/Disable Comparison, Preview Item / Add Favorite, Sell Junk, Show Hint Overlay, Interaction 2, and the map's Scroll Up, Scroll Down, Filter and Previous/Next Filter. On a controller the same actions, with the game's own names. On-screen hints follow your keys. [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/4008]No More Hard-coded Keybinds[/url] is no longer needed and can stay installed.
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kaporli/unified-keybinds/main/screenshots/new-entries.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kaporli/unified-keybinds/main/screenshots/inventory-hints.png[/img][/*]
[*][b]Controller rebinding[/b], which the game doesn't offer. Vanilla buttons use the game's names and follow your control scheme (Classic, Dynamic, Alternative), each with its own layout. Sprint (Hold), Crouch (Hold) and Scan (Toggle) get entries too. Mod actions get controller entries when a controller button triggers them. The menu shows controller buttons while you use a controller and keys when you use the keyboard.
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kaporli/unified-keybinds/main/screenshots/control-scheme-shared.png[/img][/*]
[*][b]Key combinations[/b] on every entry, vanilla included: hold one key or button and press another, for example [i]"Ctrl + K"[/i] or [i]"LB + A"[/i]. A key pressed alone is bound alone. Combinations apply after a restart, and a popup names the entries.
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kaporli/unified-keybinds/main/screenshots/combination.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kaporli/unified-keybinds/main/screenshots/prompt.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kaporli/unified-keybinds/main/screenshots/restart-popup.png[/img]
On-screen hints show the whole combination with the game's icons.
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kaporli/unified-keybinds/main/screenshots/combination-hint.png[/img][/*]
[*][b]Tap or hold on one key[/b]: a (Hold) action can share its key with another action. Tap for the other, hold for this one, for example Crouch (Hold) and Dodge/Dash on one key. It works as soon as you bind it. While the game shows a prompt on that key (talk, loot, pick up), the prompt comes first.
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kaporli/unified-keybinds/main/screenshots/shared-key.png[/img][/*]
[*][b]Conflict warning[/b]: when you apply a key that two actions active at the same time now share, a popup names the action and what it conflicts with. The side panel lists what the selected key conflicts with and is shared with, then every conflicting key of the device in view, and stays inside the menu. A key shared by actions never active together (Jump and a map's Track Waypoint on Space) is no conflict.
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kaporli/unified-keybinds/main/screenshots/conflict.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kaporli/unified-keybinds/main/screenshots/side-panel-more-cap.png[/img][/*]
[*][b]Unbind[/b] any entry, keyboard or controller: point at it and press [b]X[/b] (Square on a controller). It stays unbound across save loads and restarts. [b]Defaults[/b] brings the key back.[/*]
[*]Keys stay in sync with [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/4885]Mod Settings[/url], Native Settings UI and Redscript Configuration Framework: a change in either menu changes both, and the mod uses it right away.[/*]
[*]A changed key applies right away. Your keys are kept in a file of their own with a backup, so removing a mod or a crash doesn't cost your bindings.[/*]
[*]Never changes game or mod files, so mods that edit the settings menu keep working.[/*]
[/list]
[size=4][b]Supported keybind sources[/b][/size]

[table][tr][th]Status[/th]
[th]Keybind source[/th]
[th]Notes[/th]
[/tr]
[tr][td][b][color=#4caf50]✓ Native[/color][/b][/td]
[td][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/4575]Input Loader[/url] input file, with or without [font=Courier New]overridableUI[/font] (for example [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/5208]Let There Be Flight[/url], [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/11765]Enhanced Vehicle System[/url])[/td]
[td]Listed at startup. A key and a controller button get an entry each, also when the mod didn't make them rebindable (for example Chipware Expansion). A mod that registers its input file late through Input Loader's plugin interface may only appear from the second launch.[/td]
[/tr]
[tr][td][b][color=#4caf50]✓ Native[/color][/b][/td]
[td][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/4885]Mod Settings[/url] key option[/td]
[td]Kept in sync both ways. Key combinations stay in this menu only.[/td]
[/tr]
[tr][td][b][color=#4caf50]✓ Native[/color][/b][/td]
[td][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/30726]Redscript Configuration Framework[/url][/td]
[td]Works like [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/4575]Input Loader[/url] and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/4885]Mod Settings[/url]. Its hub key (F8) is kept in sync with RCF's Options.[/td]
[/tr]
[tr][td][b][color=#e5be37]2nd launch[/color][/b][/td]
[td][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/3518]Native Settings UI[/url][/td]
[td]Single keys. Kept in sync both ways.[/td]
[/tr]
[tr][td][b][color=#e5be37]2nd launch[/color][/b][/td]
[td][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/28308]Unified Mod Settings[/url][/td]
[td]Edits [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/3518]Native Settings UI[/url] and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/4885]Mod Settings[/url] keys, so it follows those rows.[/td]
[/tr]
[tr][td][b][color=#e5be37]2nd launch[/color][/b][/td]
[td]Mods that keep their keys in [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/30726]Redscript Configuration Framework[/url]'s hub, like the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/28390]DigitalVixen[/url] mods ([url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/29105]Shattered Chrome[/url], [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/29101]Chrome Plating[/url], [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/30508]Injuries[/url] and others)[/td]
[td]With the mod's own names. Single keys and controller buttons. Kept in sync both ways.[/td]
[/tr]
[tr][td][b][color=#4caf50]✓ Native[/color][/b][/td]
[td][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/4008]No More Hard-coded Keybinds[/url][/td]
[td]Every action it made rebindable is an entry here, so it is no longer needed. Both can stay installed, nothing is listed twice.[/td]
[/tr]
[tr][td][b][color=#4caf50]✓ Native[/color][/b][/td]
[td]Vanilla keyboard keys[/td]
[td]The game's own entries, with key combinations. A single key is also kept in the game's settings, so removing the mod keeps it.[/td]
[/tr]
[tr][td][b][color=#4caf50]✓ Native[/color][/b][/td]
[td]Vanilla controller buttons[/td]
[td]Part of the main file (was an optional file before 2.0.0). One layout per control scheme. After you change the scheme, the controller entries follow it at once.[/td]
[/tr]
[tr][td][b]⏳ Not yet[/b][/td]
[td]...[/td]
[td]If you notice a mod or framework that isn't mentioned here, [b]leave a comment[/b] and I'll look into supporting it.[/td]
[/tr]
[tr][td][b]⏳ Not yet[/b][/td]
[td][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/107]Cyber Engine Tweaks[/url] hotkeys ([font=Courier New]registerHotkey[/font], [font=Courier New]registerInput[/font])[/td]
[td]I'm still exploring a way to integrate these seamlessly.[/td]
[/tr]
[/table]
[size=4][b][color=#e5be37]Limitations[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][color=#e5be37][b]Controller: an action is listed when exactly one controller button triggers it. Movement, aiming, attacking and stick axes stay as they are.[/b][/color][/*]
[*][color=#e5be37][b]Key combinations apply after a restart. The game takes about 30 in total.[/b][/color][/*]
[*][color=#e5be37][b]No entry for the map's zoom: the mouse wheel stays as the game has it.[/b][/color][/*]
[/list]
[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Cyberpunk 2077 [b]2.5[/b][/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/2380]RED4ext[/url], [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/1511]redscript[/url], [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/4575]Input Loader[/url], [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/7780]Codeware[/url][/*]
[*]Optional, for the keys kept there: [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/4885]Mod Settings[/url], [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/107]Cyber Engine Tweaks[/url] with [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/3518]Native Settings UI[/url], [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/30726]Redscript Configuration Framework[/url][/*]
[/list]
[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]
Install with Mod Organizer 2 or Vortex, or extract into the game folder. The files go to:
[code]red4ext/plugins/ModKeybindsMenu/
bin/x64/plugins/cyber_engine_tweaks/mods/ModKeybindsMenu/init.lua[/code]
[b]Updating from 1.x[/b]: the optional file Vanilla Controller Rebinding is part of the main file now. Remove it before you install (in Mod Organizer 2 or Vortex, uninstall it), or its older script replaces the new one.
[size=4][b]Uninstallation[/b][/size]
Remove both [font=Courier New]ModKeybindsMenu[/font] folders. Optionally delete [font=Courier New]r6/cache/modkeybinds/[/font], where the mod keys are kept. Nothing is written to your save, and your game settings stay as they are. On 1.0.0, [b]start the game once with a newer version before uninstalling[/b], so your settings file gets cleaned up.

[size=4][b]Credits[/b][/size]
Uses RED4ext.SDK, pugixml and nlohmann/json. The input manager layouts and address hashes come from [url=https://github.com/jackhumbert/mod_settings]Mod Settings[/url].

[size=4][b]For mod authors[/b][/size]
Your action shows up if an [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/4575]Input Loader[/url] file gives it [font=Courier New]<button id="IK_..." overridableUI="yourActionName" />[/font], or if it is a [font=Courier New]Button[/font] mapping with a single key or key combination ([font=Courier New]buttonGroup[/font]) and no [font=Courier New]overridableUI[/font], listed under the mapping's name. A controller button in the same mapping gets a controller entry.

For nicer names, ship [font=Courier New]r6/config/modkeybinds/<YourMod>.json[/font]:
[code]{
"_section": "Your Mod",
"yourActionName": "Open Menu"
}[/code]
[font=Courier New]_section[/font] names the section for every action in that file. Names can also be [font=Courier New]LocKey#...[/font] keys.

